  "body": {
    "id": "prop:constant-score-sanity",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For any \\(P\\in\\mathcal P_{\\beta,d}(L,G,H,\\underline f,\\overline f)\\) whose \\(g\\) is constant on \\(\\mathcal X\\), every \\(M\\in\\mathfrak M_T\\) satisfies \\(C_g(M)=O_g(X)=0\\).  Hence every feasible policy has zero per-law normalized matching regret and, by Proposition \\(\\mathrm{prop:causal\\text{-}regret\\text{-}reduction}\\), zero ex ante mean conditional design-variance excess relative to the covariate prognostic oracle.",
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:pair-cost",
      "def:offline-oracle",
      "prop:causal-regret-reduction"
    ],
    "justification": "This reduction verifies that the frontier measures heterogeneous prognostic geometry rather than creating loss under a design-irrelevant score.",
    "gap": "It is the homogeneous-score reduction implicit in offline matched-pair optimality and serves as a required internal consistency check.",
    "consumer": "Applied users can verify that the cap is harmless when baseline prognosis is constant.",
    "proof_tex": "Suppose that \\(g\\) is constant on \\(\\mathcal X\\), say \\(g(x)=c\\).  Then for every edge \\((i,j)\\) of every \\(M\\in\\mathfrak M_T\\),\n\\[\n\\{g(X_i)-g(X_j)\\}^2=(c-c)^2=0.\n\\]\nDefinition \\(\\mathrm{def:pair\\text{-}cost}\\) therefore gives \\(C_g(M)=0\\) for every perfect matching \\(M\\).  Taking the minimum over \\(M\\) in Definition \\(\\mathrm{def:offline\\text{-}oracle}\\) gives \\(O_g(X)=0\\).  In particular, for every feasible \\(\\pi\\),\n\\[\nT^{-1}\\mathbb E_{P,\\xi}\\{C_g(M_\\pi)-O_g(X)\\}=0.\n\\]\nProposition \\(\\mathrm{prop:causal\\text{-}regret\\text{-}reduction}\\) identifies this quantity exactly with \\(T\\) times the ex ante mean conditional design-variance excess relative to the covariate prognostic oracle.  Hence that excess is also zero.",
